=== ROUTING_DECISIONS ===
Routing decision per field, derived from:
  - The columns actually present in `charging_telemetry` per
    migration 000171_charging_si.up.sql:
      ac_charging_power_w, dc_charging_power_w,
      ac_charging_energy_in_wh, dc_charging_energy_in_wh,
      charger_voltage_v, charger_actual_current_a,
      charger_pilot_current_a, charger_phases, battery_heater_on,
      battery_heater_power_w, charge_limit_soc_pct, charge_request,
      fast_charger_type, charging_cable_type,
      charge_port_door_open, charge_port_latch.
  - The prompt's session-level / configuration list:
      ChargeLimitSoc, ChargePortLatch, ChargePortDoorOpen,
      ChargingCableType, FastChargerType, ChargeRequest
    (ChargeRequest is not a real proto field in the charging
    category — the column charge_request is preallocated in the
    table but no charging-category Field matches it. Same for
    charger_pilot_current_a and battery_heater_power_w. These
    columns remain unused by routing.yaml until a future proto
    bump introduces matching fields.)
  - The fields referenced by name in
    `migrations/000175_caggs_and_mvs.up.sql`:
      cagg_battery_daily filters on:
        BatteryLevel, ACChargingEnergyIn, DCChargingEnergyIn,
        EnergyRemaining.

Decision tree:

  1. Field has a dedicated charging_telemetry column AND is in the
     prompt's per-tick measurement list:
       -> dest: charging_telemetry, column: <snake>
       -> also_signal_log: true if and only if the field is also
          referenced by name in cagg_battery_daily (so the cagg's
          FILTER WHERE field=<x> reads it from signal_log).
     Fields:
       ACChargingPower      -> ac_charging_power_w
       DCChargingPower      -> dc_charging_power_w
       ACChargingEnergyIn   -> ac_charging_energy_in_wh   + also_signal_log (cagg_battery_daily)
       DCChargingEnergyIn   -> dc_charging_energy_in_wh   + also_signal_log (cagg_battery_daily)
       ChargerVoltage       -> charger_voltage_v
       ChargerActualCurrent -> charger_actual_current_a
       ChargerPhases        -> charger_phases
       BatteryHeaterOn      -> battery_heater_on

  2. Field has a dedicated charging_telemetry column AND is in the
     prompt's session-level / configuration list:
       -> dest: charging_telemetry, column: <snake>
       -> also_signal_log: true (per the prompt: "fields that change
          rarely but must persist for replay").
     Fields:
       ChargeLimitSoc     -> charge_limit_soc_pct
       FastChargerType    -> fast_charger_type
       ChargingCableType  -> charging_cable_type
       ChargePortDoorOpen -> charge_port_door_open
       ChargePortLatch    -> charge_port_latch

  3. Field has NO dedicated charging_telemetry column:
       -> dest: signal_log (the cold-path catch-all per
          types.go:DestSignalLog godoc).
       -> also_signal_log NOT applicable (signal_log IS the dest).
     This is the catch-all bucket for charging-category fields the
     hot table doesn't model directly. The cagg_battery_daily
     filters on BatteryLevel and EnergyRemaining read from signal_log
     directly, so those fields land in their primary destination
     without a dual-write. ScheduledChargingStartTime and
     ScheduledDepartureTime are emitted as flattened atomic strings
     by the codec layer (compounds.go) and persist verbatim to
     signal_log; their per-component (Hour/Minute/Second) shape is
     a codec-internal detail that does not surface in routing.
     Fields (45 total):
       BMSState, BatteryLevel, BmsFullchargecomplete,
       BrickVoltageMax, BrickVoltageMin, ChargeAmps,
       ChargeCurrentRequest, ChargeCurrentRequestMax,
       ChargeEnableRequest, ChargePort, ChargePortColdWeatherMode,
